  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 102.32 Canopy",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 102.32 “Canopy” means a seasonal structure having a roof that is not designed or constructed to withstand an average snow load for the location in which it is installed, and which is erected to shelter watercraft during the boating season.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 102.33); ss by #14346, eff 8-23-25",
